<title>MALAYSIA: Malaysia national debt growing at slower rate - govt.</title>
<headline>Malaysia national debt growing at slower rate - govt.</headline>
<dateline>KUALA LUMPUR 1996-10-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Malaysia's outstanding national debt will increase an estimated 5.4 percent in 1996, after rising 14.9 percent in 1995, the Ministry of Finance said on Friday.</p>
<p>&quot;As a percentage to GNP (gross national product), the debt will be lower at 31.7 percent compared with 34 percent in 1995,&quot; the ministry said in its annual Economic Report.</p>
<p>-- Kuala Lumpur newsroom 603-201-4813</p>
